Subject: Decision needed: withdrawn application behavior
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8

We need one documented answer for employers asking to restore an application after the candidate withdrew it.

My proposal is that withdrawal remains candidate-controlled and terminal. An employer should not be able to reverse it. If the candidate returns while the job is open, they submit a new application and the old one remains in audit history.

Please confirm whether current code can enforce this before I approve the lifecycle note.

Ana

